# the tag.
#
# OUTPUT. This leg's own PyAutoFit output root,
# `output/p4_validation/validation_group_rectangular_euclid_numba_cpu_sparse/`: the output
# path omits the pin and the core count, so the shared tree would resume another run's fit.
#
# WALL-BASIS: — one row per cell this submit runs. See ../../scripts/misc/wall/README.md.
#   This submit runs ONE cell, `group/rectangular/validation/euclid_slam`. This likelihood has
#   no adopted row, so per stage the evaluations are its declared basis (EVALS_BASIS: a
#   measured count or a declared ceiling, named below), priced at Pulse's single-thread
#   per-call time over 8 Nautilus worker(s) (catalogue/pulse_lens_runtime_reference.json). No
#   adopted row measured this cell on this device, so the row is `unmeasured` and the first
#   arm IS the probe: read each stage's `wall_s / likelihood_evals` from its row.
#   - default source_lp[0] = 92550 evals (proxy: max adopted imaging
#     imaging/rectangular/hst/default/jax_gpu_sparse_fp64/hpc_a100/nautilus:source_lp[1]/seed_0);
